"description":"Blindboyboatclub is an award-winning Irish author, documentary‐maker and podcaster.\n\nAs a writer, he has published three collections of best-selling and critically-acclaimed short stories, blending myth, satire and the vernacular power of Limerick into fiction that is both darkly comic and profoundly humane. In 2026, these stories were adapted into a play “Animals” which is debuting at Ireland's national theatre, The Abbey.  \n\nHe began his podcast in 2017, combining social commentary and insightful interviews, quickly gaining a large following. He regularly tours his podcasts globally, with sell-out shows where his mix of sharp wit, empathy and social insight draws audiences into bold conversations about culture, politics and the human condition.\n\nHis screen work, including documentaries on modern slavery and the UK housing system, has won a Grierson award in 2025, an RTS award, a Sky Arts nomination and the BAFTA long list, establishing him as one of Ireland’s most distinctive documentary voices.\n\nIn this episode of Fashion Neurosis, Bella Freud and Blindboy discuss Autism, Alpha Male codes in the changing room, and if Psychoanalysis is like After-Sex talk.\n\n\nLearn more about your ad choices. Visit podcastchoices.com/adchoices", "country":"USA", "collectionViewUrl":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/podcast/fashion-neurosis-with-bella-freud/id1768794307?mt=2&uo=4", "trackViewUrl":"https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/blindboy/id1768794307?i=1000796253358&uo=4", "artworkUrl60":"https://is1-ssl.mzstatic.com/image/thumb/Podcasts221/v4/af/0c/44/af0c44b3-b5bd-2837-048f-1c842fe8693d/mza_3797900449222351589.jpeg/60x60bb.jpg", "trackTimeMillis":6695000, "contentAdvisoryRating":"Explicit", "previewUrl":"https://www.podtrac.com/pts/redirect.mp3/pdst.fm/e/pscrb.fm/rss/p/mgln.ai/e/257/traffic.megaphone.fm/VMP1291422494.mp3", "episodeUrl":"https://www.podtrac.com/pts/redirect.mp3/pdst.fm/e/pscrb.fm/rss/p/mgln.ai/e/257/traffic.megaphone.fm/VMP1291422494.mp3"